{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:22398098 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:22398098 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"22398098","source":"MED","pmid":"22398098","doi":"10.1016/j.crohns.2011.12.003","title":"Therapeutic drug monitoring of thiopurine metabolites in adult thiopurine tolerant IBD patients on maintenance therapy.","authorString":"Gilissen LP, Wong DR, Engels LG, Bierau J, Bakker JA, Paulussen AD, Romberg-Camps MJ, Stronkhorst A, Bus P, Bos LP, Hooymans PM, Stockbrügger RW, Neef C, Masclee AA.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Gilissen LP","firstName":"Lennard P L","lastName":"Gilissen","initials":"LP","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology and Hepatology, Catharina Hospital, Eindhoven, The Netherlands. lennard.gilissen@cze.nl"}]}},{"fullName":"Wong DR","firstName":"Dennis R","lastName":"Wong","initials":"DR"},{"fullName":"Engels LG","firstName":"Leopold G J B","lastName":"Engels","initials":"LG"},{"fullName":"Bierau J","firstName":"Jörgen","lastName":"Bierau","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1329-5381"}},{"fullName":"Bakker JA","firstName":"Jaap A","lastName":"Bakker","initials":"JA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2918-7361"}},{"fullName":"Paulussen AD","firstName":"Aimée D C","lastName":"Paulussen","initials":"AD"},{"fullName":"Romberg-Camps MJ","firstName":"Mariëlle J","lastName":"Romberg-Camps","initials":"MJ"},{"fullName":"Stronkhorst A","firstName":"Arnold","lastName":"Stronkhorst","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Bus P","firstName":"Paul","lastName":"Bus","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Bos LP","firstName":"Laurens P","lastName":"Bos","initials":"LP"},{"fullName":"Hooymans PM","firstName":"Piet M","lastName":"Hooymans","initials":"PM"},{"fullName":"Stockbrügger RW","firstName":"Reinhold W","lastName":"Stockbrügger","initials":"RW"},{"fullName":"Neef C","firstName":"Cees","lastName":"Neef","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Masclee AA","firstName":"Ad A M","lastName":"Masclee","initials":"AA"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2918-7361"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1329-5381"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"6","volume":"6","journalIssueId":1941609,"dateOfPublication":"2012 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2012,"printPublicationDate":"2012-07-01","journal":{"title":"Journal of Crohn's & colitis","medlineAbbreviation":"J Crohns Colitis","isoabbreviation":"J Crohns Colitis","nlmid":"101318676","essn":"1876-4479","issn":"1873-9946"}},"pubYear":"2012","pageInfo":"698-707","abstractText":"<h4>Background and aims</h4>Therapeutic drug monitoring of active metabolites of thiopurines, azathioprine and 6-mercaptopurine, is relatively new. The proposed therapeutic threshold level of the active 6-thioguanine nucleotides (6-TGN) is ≥235 pmol/8×10(8) erythrocytes. The aim of this prospective cross-sectional study was to compare 6-TGN levels in adult thiopurine tolerant IBD patients with an exacerbation with those in remission, and to determine the therapeutic 6-TGN cut-off level.<h4>Methods</h4>Hundred IBD patients were included. Outcome measures were thiopurine metabolite levels, calculated therapeutic 6-TGN cut-off level, CDAI/CAI scores, thiopurine dose and TPMT enzyme activity.<h4>Results</h4>Forty-one patients had an exacerbation, 59 patients were in remission. In 17% of all patients 6-TGN levels were compatible with non-compliance. The median 6-TGN levels were not significantly different between the exacerbation and remission group (227 versus 263 pmol/8×10(8) erythrocytes, p=0.29). The previous reported therapeutic 6-TGN cut-off level of 235 pmol/8×10(8) erythrocytes was confirmed in this study. Twenty-six of the 41 patients (63%) with active disease had 6-TGN levels below this threshold and 24 of 59 IBD patients (41%) in clinical remission (p=0.04).<h4>Conclusions</h4>Thiopurine non-compliance occurs frequently both in active and quiescent disease. 6-TGN levels below or above the therapeutic threshold are associated with a significant higher chance of IBD exacerbation and remission, respectively. These data support the role of therapeutic drug monitoring in thiopurine maintenance therapy in IBD to reveal non-compliance or underdosing, and can be used as a practical tool to optimize thiopurine therapy, especially in case of thiopurine non-response.","affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology and Hepatology, Catharina Hospital, Eindhoven, The Netherlands. lennard.gilissen@cze.nl","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Comparative Study","Clinical Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Inflammatory Bowel Diseases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Disease Progression"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Azathioprine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Methyltransferases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Thioinosine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AA","qualifierName":"analogs & derivatives","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"BL","qualifierName":"blood","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_Y